   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Cong Chevra Kadisha Anash, Inc. of Monroe to file an application for a real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S7808",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7808-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7808\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing Cong Chevra Kadisha\nAnash, Inc. of Monroe to file an application for a real property tax\nexemption\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo allow the Congregation Chevra Kadisha Anash to apply for a real\nproperty tax exemption after the applicable taxable status date.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows the assessor of the Town of Monroe, in Orange County,\nto accept and review an application from the Congregation Chevra\nKadisha Anash of Monroe for a nonprofit real property tax exemption\nfor the 2010 and 2011 assessment roll, as if it had been received on\nor before the applicable taxable status date.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Congregation Chevra Kadisha Anash is a non-profit organization\nthat would be otherwise entitled to an exemption under section 420-a\nof the Real Property Tax Law had the organization filed an application\nfor the exemption by the appropriate taxable status date.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
